   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to including the lakes of Drew\nand South in Putnam county within the definition of \"inland waterways\" for the\npurposes of waterfront revitalization",
    "basePrintNo": "S5828",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5828-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5828\n\nSPONSOR: SERINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to\nincluding the lakes of Drew and South in Putnam county within the defi-\nnition of \"inland waterways\" for the purposes of waterfront revitaliza-\ntion\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to designate certain lakes in the\ntown of Kent as inland waterways.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Paragraph (a) of subdivision 911 of the Executive Law is\namended by adding Drew and South Lakes to the list of New York State's\nmajor inland lakes.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective dates.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is in response to a request from the Town of Kent to\ndesignate the following lakes (Drew and South)as major inland lakes.\n\nSuch a designation would allow Kent to participate in the Coastal and\nInland Waterways Program, and apply for grants through the Local Water-\nfront Revitalization Program (LWRP). The LWRP can help communities\naddress waterfront redevelopment, expansion of visual and physical\npublic access to the water, coastal resource protection and other water\ndependent uses such as boating, fishing and swimming.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
