    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5828A\n\nSPONSOR: SERINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to including the lake of\nDrew within the definition of \"inland waterways\" for the purposes of\nwaterfront revitalization\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to designate Drew Lake in the town of\nKent as inland waterways.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Paragraph (a) of subdivision 911 of the Executive Law is\namended by adding Drew Lake to the list of New York State's major inland\nlakes.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective dates.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is in response to a request from the Town of Kent to\ndesignate the following Drew Lake as a major inland lake.  Such a desig-\nnation would allow Kent to participate in the Coastal and Inland Water-\nways Program, and apply for grants through the Local Waterfront Revital-\nization Program (LWRP). The LWRP can help communities address waterfront\nredevelopment, expansion of visual and physical public access to the\nwater, coastal resource protection and other water dependent uses such\nas boating, fishing and swimming.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
